cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioReservoir: public connectomes as fixed reservoirs"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its experiment protocols, please cite it. The connectome datasets it
  consumes have their own citations, listed in NOTICE and docs/DATA.md — cite those too.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Golubev
    given-names: Igor
    affiliation: "IG Digital Lab (IGGO, LLC), Sacramento, CA, USA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/igdigitallab/bioreservoir"
url: "https://fly.igdigi.com"
abstract: >-
  BioReservoir treats a published whole-brain connectome as a fixed reservoir: the wiring is loaded
  as a signed graph, simulated as a leaky integrate-and-fire spiking network, driven with encoded
  input and read out without training the network itself. Every experiment is pre-registered with
  an OpenTimestamps proof and ships controls — a degree-preserving rewired graph, an Erdos-Renyi
  graph, a no-connectome baseline and a seeded coin flip. Experiment 001 uses the male (MaleCNS
  v1.0) and female (BANC) Drosophila connectomes.
keywords:
  - connectome
  - reservoir computing
  - spiking neural network
  - Drosophila
  - computational neuroscience
  - pre-registration
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
